# Restart autopilot after changes

When you edit backend or frontend code in this project, restart the local server before ending your turn so the user can test right away.

## Command

From the repo root, run:

```powershell
.venv\Scripts\python scripts\restart_autopilot.py
```

Use `--build` if you changed frontend code and want to force a rebuild:

```powershell
.venv\Scripts\python scripts\restart_autopilot.py --build
```

## What it does

1. Stops any process on port 8000
2. Rebuilds `frontend/dist` when source is newer than the last build (or when `--build` is passed)
3. Starts uvicorn detached and opens http://127.0.0.1:8000

## Skip only when

- The user explicitly asks not to restart
- You made no runnable code changes (docs-only, comments-only, etc.)
